{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:17483457 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:17483457 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"17483457","source":"MED","pmid":"17483457","pmcid":"PMC1895982","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC1895982"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.0611364104","title":"A-803467, a potent and selective Nav1.8 sodium channel blocker, attenuates neuropathic and inflammatory pain in the rat.","authorString":"Jarvis MF, Honore P, Shieh CC, Chapman M, Joshi S, Zhang XF, Kort M, Carroll W, Marron B, Atkinson R, Thomas J, Liu D, Krambis M, Liu Y, McGaraughty S, Chu K, Roeloffs R, Zhong C, Mikusa JP, Hernandez G, Gauvin D, Wade C, Zhu C, Pai M, Scanio M, Shi L, Drizin I, Gregg R, Matulenko M, Hakeem A, Gross M, Johnson M, Marsh K, Wagoner PK, Sullivan JP, Faltynek CR, Krafte DS.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Jarvis MF","lastName":"Jarvis","firstName":"Michael F","initials":"MF","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Neuroscience Research, Abbott Laboratories, Abbott Park, IL 60064, USA. michael.jarvis@abbott.com"}]}},{"fullName":"Honore P","lastName":"Honore","firstName":"Prisca","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Shieh CC","lastName":"Shieh","firstName":"Char-Chang","initials":"CC"},{"fullName":"Chapman M","lastName":"Chapman","firstName":"Mark","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-8699-3334"}},{"fullName":"Joshi S","lastName":"Joshi","firstName":"Shailen","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Zhang XF","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Xu-Feng","initials":"XF"},{"fullName":"Kort M","lastName":"Kort","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Carroll W","lastName":"Carroll","firstName":"William","initials":"W"},{"fullName":"Marron B","lastName":"Marron","firstName":"Brian","initials":"B"},{"fullName":"Atkinson R","lastName":"Atkinson","firstName":"Robert","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Thomas J","lastName":"Thomas","firstName":"James","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Liu D","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Dong","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Krambis M","lastName":"Krambis","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Liu Y","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Yi","initials":"Y"},{"fullName":"McGaraughty S","lastName":"McGaraughty","firstName":"Steve","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Chu K","lastName":"Chu","firstName":"Katharine","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Roeloffs R","lastName":"Roeloffs","firstName":"Rosemarie","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Zhong C","lastName":"Zhong","firstName":"Chengmin","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Mikusa JP","lastName":"Mikusa","firstName":"Joseph P","initials":"JP"},{"fullName":"Hernandez G","lastName":"Hernandez","firstName":"Gricelda","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Gauvin D","lastName":"Gauvin","firstName":"Donna","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Wade C","lastName":"Wade","firstName":"Carrie","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Zhu C","lastName":"Zhu","firstName":"Chang","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Pai M","lastName":"Pai","firstName":"Madhavi","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Scanio M","lastName":"Scanio","firstName":"Marc","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Shi L","lastName":"Shi","firstName":"Lei","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Drizin I","lastName":"Drizin","firstName":"Irene","initials":"I"},{"fullName":"Gregg R","lastName":"Gregg","firstName":"Robert","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Matulenko M","lastName":"Matulenko","firstName":"Mark","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Hakeem A","lastName":"Hakeem","firstName":"Ahmed","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Gross M","lastName":"Gross","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Johnson M","lastName":"Johnson","firstName":"Matthew","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Marsh K","lastName":"Marsh","firstName":"Kennan","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Wagoner PK","lastName":"Wagoner","firstName":"P Kay","initials":"PK"},{"fullName":"Sullivan JP","lastName":"Sullivan","firstName":"James P","initials":"JP"},{"fullName":"Faltynek CR","lastName":"Faltynek","firstName":"Connie R","initials":"CR"},{"fullName":"Krafte DS","lastName":"Krafte","firstName":"Douglas S","initials":"DS"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-8699-3334"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"20","volume":"104","journalIssueId":1396521,"dateOfPublication":"2007 May","monthOfPublication":5,"yearOfPublication":2007,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","nlmid":"7505876"},"printPublicationDate":"2007-05-01"},"pubYear":"2007","pageInfo":"8520-8525","abstractText":"Activation of tetrodotoxin-resistant sodium channels contributes to action potential electrogenesis in neurons. Antisense oligonucleotide studies directed against Na(v)1.8 have shown that this channel contributes to experimental inflammatory and neuropathic pain. We report here the discovery of A-803467, a sodium channel blocker that potently blocks tetrodotoxin-resistant currents (IC(50) = 140 nM) and the generation of spontaneous and electrically evoked action potentials in vitro in rat dorsal root ganglion neurons. In recombinant cell lines, A-803467 potently blocked human Na(v)1.8 (IC(50) = 8 nM) and was >100-fold selective vs. human Na(v)1.2, Na(v)1.3, Na(v)1.5, and Na(v)1.7 (IC(50) values >or=1 microM). A-803467 (20 mg/kg, i.v.) blocked mechanically evoked firing of wide dynamic range neurons in the rat spinal dorsal horn. A-803467 also dose-dependently reduced mechanical allodynia in a variety of rat pain models including: spinal nerve ligation (ED(50) = 47 mg/kg, i.p.), sciatic nerve injury (ED(50) = 85 mg/kg, i.p.), capsaicin-induced secondary mechanical allodynia (ED(50) approximately 100 mg/kg, i.p.), and thermal hyperalgesia after intraplantar complete Freund's adjuvant injection (ED(50) = 41 mg/kg, i.p.). A-803467 was inactive against formalin-induced nociception and acute thermal and postoperative pain. These data demonstrate that acute and selective pharmacological blockade of Na(v)1.8 sodium channels in vivo produces significant antinociception in animal models of neuropathic and inflammatory pain.","affiliation":"Neuroscience Research, Abbott Laboratories, Abbott Park, IL 60064, USA. michael.jarvis@abbott.com","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ganglia, Spinal","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Neurons","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rats"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rats, Sprague-Dawley"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pain","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mononeuropathies","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Inflammation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aniline Compounds","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AD","qualifierName":"administration & dosage"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation"